1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,185
This is the Great Wall of China.

2
00:00:02,385 --> 00:00:04,459
The year is fifteen seventy.

3
00:00:04,659 --> 00:00:07,012
Every fire you see means one thing.

4
00:00:07,212 --> 00:00:08,645
Enemies are coming.

5
00:00:08,844 --> 00:00:10,983
And the guy who lit the first one?

6
00:00:11,183 --> 00:00:12,124
That's me.

7
00:00:12,324 --> 00:00:13,919
And there was no enemy.

8
00:00:14,119 --> 00:00:15,997
At least, I thought there wasn't.

9
00:00:16,397 --> 00:00:17,667
Let me rewind.

10
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:22,627
Hi.

11
00:00:22,827 --> 00:00:24,020
It's me again.

12
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:25,749
The red cap guy.

13
00:00:25,949 --> 00:00:30,972
Last time, I touched a magic pocket watch and messed up three centuries of history.

14
00:00:31,172 --> 00:00:33,225
So I made myself a promise.

15
00:00:33,425 --> 00:00:35,553
No more touching museum stuff.

16
00:00:36,153 --> 00:00:38,705
Two weeks later, I was back at the museum.

17
00:00:38,905 --> 00:00:41,717
New exhibit: Treasures of the Ming Dynasty.

18
00:00:41,917 --> 00:00:45,048
And in the middle of the room, one single, dusty brick.

19
00:00:45,248 --> 00:00:45,975
Old.

20
00:00:46,175 --> 00:00:46,878
Grey.

21
00:00:47,078 --> 00:00:47,835
Boring.

22
00:00:48,035 --> 00:00:50,024
The sign said: Do not touch.

23
00:00:50,524 --> 00:00:52,347
I lasted four seconds.

24
00:00:52,847 --> 00:00:54,516
The brick started to glow.

25
00:00:54,716 --> 00:00:56,131
The floor vanished.

26
00:00:56,331 --> 00:00:59,681
And I fell four hundred and fifty years into the past.

27
00:01:00,181 --> 00:01:03,162
I landed on a mountain ridge in northern China.

28
00:01:03,362 --> 00:01:08,492
And in front of me, climbing over the peaks like a giant stone dragon, was the Great Wall.

29
00:01:09,092 --> 00:01:11,276
Here's the first thing they don't tell you.

30
00:01:11,476 --> 00:01:12,860
It's not one wall.

31
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:18,398
It's many walls, built and rebuilt by different dynasties over more than two thousand years.

32
00:01:18,598 --> 00:01:23,028
Put all the pieces together, and you get over twenty one thousand kilometres.

33
00:01:23,228 --> 00:01:25,426
That's about halfway around the Earth.

34
00:01:26,026 --> 00:01:28,605
The part I landed on was brand new.

35
00:01:28,805 --> 00:01:32,570
The Ming dynasty was rebuilding the wall in stone and brick.

36
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:40,676
And a famous general named Qi Jiguang was adding tall, hollow watchtowers, so soldiers could live right on top of the wall.

37
00:01:41,276 --> 00:01:44,573
Thousands of workers were hauling bricks up the mountain.

38
00:01:44,773 --> 00:01:47,258
Soldiers, farmers, even prisoners.

39
00:01:47,458 --> 00:01:50,939
And many bricks were stamped with a mark: who made them, and where.

40
00:01:51,139 --> 00:01:53,968
If a brick cracked, they knew exactly who to blame.

41
00:01:54,568 --> 00:01:57,454
A foreman handed me a stamp and a fresh brick.

42
00:01:57,654 --> 00:01:59,083
Your mark, he said.

43
00:01:59,283 --> 00:02:00,991
I can't write Chinese.

44
00:02:01,191 --> 00:02:04,029
So I drew the only thing I know how to draw.

45
00:02:04,229 --> 00:02:05,396
A tiny cap.

46
00:02:05,596 --> 00:02:07,035
Remember that brick.

47
00:02:07,635 --> 00:02:09,159
Then I smelled lunch.

48
00:02:09,359 --> 00:02:11,831
A giant pot of steaming sticky rice.

49
00:02:12,031 --> 00:02:13,342
I was starving.

50
00:02:13,542 --> 00:02:15,946
I grabbed a bowl, and the cook screamed.

51
00:02:16,145 --> 00:02:17,887
That rice wasn't lunch.

52
00:02:18,087 --> 00:02:19,159
It was glue.

53
00:02:19,759 --> 00:02:23,532
Ming builders mixed sticky rice soup with lime to make mortar.

54
00:02:23,732 --> 00:02:29,053
Scientists today found that the rice makes it remarkably strong and water resistant.

55
00:02:29,253 --> 00:02:33,468
Some of those walls are still standing, about five hundred years later.

56
00:02:34,068 --> 00:02:35,933
And I, of course, tripped.

57
00:02:36,133 --> 00:02:38,796
A whole sack of rice went into the mortar.

58
00:02:38,996 --> 00:02:40,157
Double sticky.

59
00:02:40,357 --> 00:02:42,303
The foreman's face turned red.

60
00:02:42,503 --> 00:02:45,683
Then he shrugged, and slapped it between the bricks anyway.

61
00:02:46,283 --> 00:02:47,163
Night fell.

62
00:02:47,363 --> 00:02:49,669
The wind on that mountain was brutal.

63
00:02:49,869 --> 00:02:54,489
I hid inside a beacon tower, and found a big pile of dry straw and wood.

64
00:02:54,689 --> 00:02:55,706
And a torch.

65
00:02:55,906 --> 00:02:57,385
Perfect, I thought.

66
00:02:57,585 --> 00:02:58,729
A campfire.

67
00:02:59,229 --> 00:03:01,086
That was not a campfire.

68
00:03:01,286 --> 00:03:03,208
That was the alarm system.

69
00:03:03,408 --> 00:03:06,831
The moment my fire flared up, the next tower lit theirs.

70
00:03:07,031 --> 00:03:08,058
Then the next.

71
00:03:08,258 --> 00:03:09,163
And the next.

72
00:03:09,363 --> 00:03:13,506
A chain of fire racing across the mountains, faster than any horse.

73
00:03:14,106 --> 00:03:15,687
The Ming had a code.

74
00:03:15,887 --> 00:03:19,743
One fire and one cannon shot meant about a hundred raiders.

75
00:03:19,943 --> 00:03:21,822
Two fires, five hundred.

76
00:03:22,022 --> 00:03:24,239
Three fires, a thousand or more.

77
00:03:24,439 --> 00:03:27,304
Thanks to the wind, I had accidentally lit three.

78
00:03:27,904 --> 00:03:28,658
Drums.

79
00:03:28,858 --> 00:03:29,693
Horns.

80
00:03:29,893 --> 00:03:33,149
Soldiers pouring onto the wall in the middle of the night.

81
00:03:33,349 --> 00:03:36,940
And me, standing next to the biggest fire, holding a torch.

82
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,426
I was going to be in so much trouble.

83
00:03:40,026 --> 00:03:42,863
And then a soldier pointed into the dark valley.

84
00:03:43,063 --> 00:03:49,115
Down below, caught in the light of my fire, was a band of raiders with ladders, creeping toward the wall.

85
00:03:49,315 --> 00:03:52,388
Right under the part I had glued with double rice.

86
00:03:52,988 --> 00:03:55,045
They threw up hooks and ladders.

87
00:03:55,245 --> 00:03:56,025
They pushed.

88
00:03:56,225 --> 00:03:57,184
They pulled.

89
00:03:57,384 --> 00:03:59,263
But that section didn't move.

90
00:03:59,463 --> 00:04:00,768
Not one brick.

91
00:04:00,968 --> 00:04:06,533
The raiders looked at the army above them, looked at the very sticky wall, and decided to go home.

92
00:04:07,133 --> 00:04:08,747
The soldiers cheered.

93
00:04:08,947 --> 00:04:12,757
The officers praised whoever had raised the alarm so fast.

94
00:04:12,957 --> 00:04:15,471
Nobody asked who lit the first fire.

95
00:04:15,671 --> 00:04:17,188
I didn't volunteer.

96
00:04:17,788 --> 00:04:25,708
A year later, in fifteen seventy one, the Ming made peace with the Mongol leader Altan Khan, and the border grew calmer for decades.

97
00:04:25,908 --> 00:04:27,720
I'd like to think I helped.

98
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,634
I definitely didn't.

99
00:04:30,234 --> 00:04:31,923
Oh, and one more thing.

100
00:04:32,123 --> 00:04:35,739
You've probably heard that the Great Wall is visible from space.

101
00:04:35,939 --> 00:04:36,900
It isn't.

102
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,848
Not with the naked eye.

103
00:04:39,048 --> 00:04:44,598
In two thousand and three, China's first astronaut, Yang Liwei, looked for it, and couldn't see it.

104
00:04:45,198 --> 00:04:48,010
Then the brick in my pocket started to glow again.

105
00:04:48,410 --> 00:04:49,897
Back in the museum.

106
00:04:50,097 --> 00:04:51,281
Same exhibit.

107
00:04:51,481 --> 00:04:53,259
Same dusty Ming brick.

108
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:55,477
But this time, I looked closer.

109
00:04:55,677 --> 00:04:59,335
In the corner, next to the maker's mark, was a tiny little cap.

110
00:05:00,135 --> 00:05:03,426
So no, I didn't destroy the Great Wall of China.

111
00:05:03,626 --> 00:05:07,347
I set it on fire, filled it with rice, and almost started a war.

112
00:05:07,547 --> 00:05:09,161
But it's still standing.

113
00:05:09,361 --> 00:05:10,446
You're welcome.

114
00:05:11,246 --> 00:05:13,283
Next time, I'm staying home.

115
00:05:13,483 --> 00:05:14,447
Probably.
